<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Skomantas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Skomantas was a leader of the Sudovians, or Yotvingians, a Baltic people, in the later 13th century. He led raids on Rus' and Polish lands and resisted the advance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, but in 1283 he submitted to the Order, ending organised Sudovian resistance. Many of his people were then resettled in Sambia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/skomantas.jpg" alt="Skomantas" width="241" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Radzivon Panschwitz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Komantas_of_Yotvingia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
